{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1523481-slashers-in-the-reckoning","id":1523481,"title":"Slashers in the Reckoning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-02T17:09:45-07:00","id":1523481,"title":"Slashers in the Reckoning","content":"The basics of this thread is an extremely simple hack: retooling <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b> to handle slashers. Conceptually, a Slasher comes about through a variation of Imbuing, with the difference being that the \u201cMessengers\u201d who Imbue Slashers are enemies of the Messengers who Imbue Hunters, who have figured out how the Imbuement process works and applied it to people who have a predilection for murder.<br /> <br /> In my first draft for this idea, Slashers are identical to Hunters, save only for the fact that they turn their talents against humans instead of monsters. This means that this idea requires you to use either the original <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b>, or <b>H5</b> with the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/418098\" target=\"_blank\">Imbued</a> STV supplement. Even if you're running <b>H5</b> <i>without</i> Imbued, you'll need that supplement for the Slashers. Though in that case, you lose the idea that \u201canti-Messengers\u201d are attempting to undermine the Messengers' plans. Instead, they \u201cmerely\u201d become another mysterious evil force that's found another way to mess with humanity.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> wonder if it would make sense to replace Creeds with something patterned after the Undertakings of Chronicles of Darkness's Slashers; and if so, what other changes would need to be done to comport with that change. And in 1e, Mercy isn't appropriate for Slashers; so at least one of the Virtues would need to be replaced, probably along with Mercy-based Creeds and Edges. H5 doesn't have that issue, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2024, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T21:25:32-07:00","id":1523485,"title":"","content":"For retooling Undertakings into Creeds, Avengers work pretty much as-is. So could Charmers and Virtuosos if we squint a bit. Brutes and Undesirables are harder.<br /> <br /> &quot;Slasher Virtues&quot; could be Anti-Virtues; subverted and twisted forms of the Virtues. <b>Anti-Zeal</b> is firm intolerance against the &quot;wrong&quot;, but borne out of blind fear and hatred. <b>Anti-Vision</b> is the desire to seek the truth, but working on tunnel vision and sharpshooter fallacy. <b>Anti-Mercy</b> is respectful tolerance, but only for minute criteria of worthiness that the slasher personally sympathizes with, rather than a broader sense of goodness.<br /> <br /> ... Okay so that sounds like what a lot of 'fallen' or 'deranged' hunters end up doing/being. Ehhh. Maybe the Imbued risk inverting their Virtues into Anti-Virtues with their equivalent of breaking points, and when all three Virtues are subverted, they become Slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T22:56:49-07:00","id":1523486,"title":"","content":"You already have them. They're called Waywards, if you're looking for Imbued that hunt humans for whatever reason, or you can use gorehound fomori, which cornered that niche in the WoD back in 2e Werewolf at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T00:38:35-07:00","id":1523487,"title":"","content":"Very good question and responses!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T15:06:23-07:00","id":1523740,"title":"","content":"While Gorehounds are good (especially if you mix original and &quot;Take 2&quot; varieties), I presume the goal here is to 1) center the Hunter side of things rather than the Werewolf, and 2) provide a framework for more involved Slasher creation rules. A dark equivalent of Hunters that share the same complexity.<br /> <br /> Although I will say that Gorehounds, being Fomori, DO serve the Wyrm, which can charitably be called an enemy to the Messengers. The Messengers ARE trying to deal with the evils that plague the world, and the Wyrm is arguably head-honcho in this department.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T18:51:43-07:00","id":1523749,"title":"","content":"Fomori in general have the benefit of being frighteningly odd and diverse and also likely to freak out Imbued because they rapidly change back into normal-looking people (well, corpses) if they die. Just make sure not to kill the cell with a one-off Throwback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T07:49:06-07:00","id":1523878,"title":"","content":"Fomori are all well and good; and if you want to use them, go for it! But that's something different from what's being discussed here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}